- Semantic unit checks of the ref-model copy (empty state, accept, hold-stall with `s_ready=0`, no-overwrite-under-stall, simultaneous consume+load, ordering, drain) — all pass.
- A stub-based smoke harness fed transactions from (a) a faithful model of the intentionally-buggy RTL and (b) a corrected DUT delegating to an **independent** oracle copy: the scoreboard flagged 8 mismatches covering all three documented RTL bugs (bug #2 `m_valid` stuck high right after reset, bug #1 `s_ready` always 1, bug #3 payload overwritten while stalled) and passed 13/13 with zero false positives on the corrected side.

